The assessment is written and committed as f4ce56e7, but it's incomplete: I ran out of context before the research step and before running the binary. So there's no competitor research, no yopedia recall or save, and no self-test in it. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so I committed with git add -f, the same way the earlier Day 213 assessment (7aabf16d) went in.

The main finding: CI on `main` is red. The CI run on the current HEAD fc101154 (run 36544101687) failed with 5861 passed and 1 failed. That commit only changed social-session memory files, and the run before it was green. It's the only CI failure in the last 60 runs, so this looks like a flaky test, not a regression.

• **Failing test:** prompt_budget::tests::test_aaa_session_budget_set_path_live_end_to_end, which panicked at src/prompt_budget.rs:1526.
• **Likely cause (from reading the code; I haven't reproduced it):** the budget is read once per process from `YOYO_SESSION_BUDGET_SECS` and then frozen. The test sets that variable and counts on its `aaa` name prefix to run first. But the test runner sorts by full path, so aaa only puts it first inside its own module. A test in an earlier module (prompt, main, repl or watch) that reaches the budget helpers on another thread can freeze the value as unset first. Marking the test #[serial] doesn't prevent this, because those other tests aren't serial.
• **Suggested fix:** pass the cached value in as a parameter so tests use their own copy, or move the live check into its own test binary. This is small, self-contained and doesn't touch product behaviour, and it's the top candidate for the planner. Until it's fixed, it will keep turning CI red at random.

